WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
Fire tiny, fast alpha particles
at a very thin sheet of metal

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:05.670
foil.

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:07.990
Almost all of them
sail straight through,

4
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.990
as if nothing were there at all.

5
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.610
But a few are knocked
sharply off course,

6
00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.050
and a very small number
bounce straight back.

7
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.910
What must the inside
of an atom be like?

8
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.950
In this mission, you'll follow
how the model of the atom

9
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.050
changed, from tiny solid
spheres to the plum pudding,

10
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.280
then the nuclear model,
and electrons in shells.

11
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.870
You'll see why scientists change
a model when new evidence

12
00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:33.710
arrives.

13
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.670
And you'll learn how the
electrons in an atom are arranged.

14
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: explain what the
scattering experiment revealed

15
00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.910
about atoms.
